# Screening: The Paper Lantern, `screen-cut-v4` (director release, asset `paper-lantern-cut-v4.mp4`, editor cut-v4 @378db12)

## How I watched
- Downloaded the asset (sha256 starts 493be6275c84, matches the release note); ffprobe: H.264 1280x720 24 fps + AAC stereo, 20.000 s.
- Picture: I compared the framemd5 of the video stream with cut-v3's (the one I screened): **identical**, so my cut-v3 picture notes (`screenings/screen-cut-v3.md`) stand unchanged. I did not re-watch frames.
- Sound: **I did not hear it.** The listening service still returns HTTP 429 (retry in ~7 h), so I measured v4 against v3 (ebur128, bands, cricket-band envelope, click scan, stereo, edges, faster-whisper for voice).

## Sound, measured, v4 against v3
- Integrated -16.1 LUFS, LRA 2.1 LU, true peak -4.5 dBFS (v3 -3.9), sample peak 0.60: no clipping, same loudness, slightly more headroom.
- Length unchanged (882,471 samples). Fades up from silence (first 50 ms peak 0.008) and out to silence (last 50 ms peak 0.002). No abrupt edge.
- River rumble tamed: the 40-150 Hz band is ~10 dB lower than v3 (-39 vs -30 dBFS RMS), 150-500 Hz about 1.5 dB lower; 500 Hz-1.5 kHz is ~1.4 dB higher (the added bubbling texture). Overall per-2-s level follows the same gentle swell as before (within ~1 dB of v3 at each 2 s).
- Crickets: in the 3-6.5 kHz band v4 is ~2 dB louder than v3 at the start (-34 vs -36 dB at 0-2 s, -29 vs -32 at 2-6 s) and thins the same way toward the end (-42 dB at 18-20 s). Its envelope is now strongly pulsed (dominant modulation ~38 Hz and peaks about 8.7x the median, against a ~19 Hz tremolo and 5.4x in v3), which is a chirp-pulse train rather than a steady tremolo; this agrees with the director's report that it now reads as insects. Whether it sounds like crickets to an ear I cannot say.
- Clicks: largest sample step 0.17 (same as v3, at the 06 s dissolve; no click found there in v3 either). On 2 ms windows of the >3 kHz band the loudest transient is 4.6x its surroundings at ~02.05 s (a cricket-sized blip, far short of a click) and nothing else is higher. No click found.
- Voice: faster-whisper `tiny` returns only " ." at 0.0 s (no_speech_prob 0.37); v3 returned " You" from the same fade-in noise. No sign of voice.
- Stereo: channels nearly uncorrelated (corr 0.07), wide and diffuse as before; mono fold-down unchecked.
- Music: not changed per the director's note; I did not re-measure it separately.

## Anything that would stop a lock?
Not from what I can measure or see: picture is the same as cut-v3 (nothing confused or dragged, notes 1-3 resolved), the sound has no clipping, click, voice or abrupt edge, and the crickets are pulsed. The one gap is unchanged: nobody has *heard* the mix, so "pleasant and soft" and "sounds like crickets rather than hiss" rest on measurements and the director's classifier listen. Lock on measurements and say so if the listening service stays out.
